@@ -333,6 +333,7 @@ Dispatch metadata (`roles/goldfish.md` GF-01 field 6, critic variant):
 - **Tool budget (hard cap, first-class field):** {{TOOL_BUDGET default: "≤30 tool uses"}} for the review itself, plus a **closing allowance of +5 tool uses** spendable on closing only (mechanics under "Closing allowance" in the report-format section below). The stated number is the base cap: reaching it ends the REVIEW, not the dispatch — stop reviewing there, then close out through the allowance. Never carry the review itself past the base cap. **Shipped harness limit and effective working cap:** the selected Critic agent definition (`plugins/pipeline-core/agents/critic.md`) ships `maxTurns: 100`. The guard reserves five closing calls and ten safety calls, so its effective working cap is at most 85: `min(briefed base cap, 100 − 5 − 10)`. The default base cap here remains 30, with five closing calls; a briefed base cap of 85 uses the full effective working allowance. Neither 85 nor 30 is the shipped `maxTurns` value. If an actual selected definition differs, derive its working cap from that definition and retain the closing/safety reserve. **Runner support:** Claude Code's installed hook counts authenticated subagent calls and restricts an over-cap review to closing acts. The runner-neutral policy core is shipped for other adapters, but Codex and Antigravity do not yet provide authenticated live-call adapters, so on those runners the base cap remains a briefing duty rather than an enforced count. Do not claim cross-runner enforcement from the shared core alone. `maxTurns` itself is a real harness cliff wherever the runner exposes it — treat reaching it as data loss, not merely a missed target (`backlog/items/2026-08-23-briefed-tool-budget-sits-below-an-unannounced-harness-maxturns-cliff.md`).
 - **80 % checkpoint (all runners, all dispatches):** at about 80 % of the base tool budget, if the task is not done, stop editing, commit what is already green, write an interim report (done / remaining / next step) into the dispatch record (Critic: into its own `critic-notes.md`) and end the turn with that report; the dispatcher decides whether to grant more budget or dispatch a follow-up. Claude enforces this with a hook notice from `guard-dispatch-budget.mjs`; Codex and Antigravity have no authenticated budget adapter yet, so there it is this briefing duty.
 - {{ADVISOR_DEMAND_LINE: if the Elephant has a current bounded Advisor demand, include verbatim: "Do not invoke or reuse the Advisor; consultation ownership remains with the Elephant" (MP-26) — else delete this line.}}
+- {{RISKS_WITHOUT_BEHAVIOUR_LINE: ONLY when the Spec's risk trace table lists risks that no test path, command or stated residual covers (derived on read by `inspectSpecRiskTrace`, ids only), replace this whole line with `risks without behaviour: <ids>; inspect whether the delivered behaviour or a stated residual covers each`; otherwise delete this line. Never add Spec prose or a characterization.}}
 
